mendations for  example  and a few days ago some cantons changed  some of the rules uh reintroducing masks  in some indoor spaces or in schools for  example and because of the federal uh  situation in switzerland it's the  cantons who would make changes first the  government is quite reluctant to  introduce national measures  so those rules looking to stay in place  for the moment joe faye and bern thank  you very much  france's minister for overseas  territories is on his way to martinique  in guadalupe following days of violent  protests on the caribbean islands the  french government has vowed a firm  response to the unrest local opposition  to covert 19 measures imposed by paris  is adding to long-standing grievances  over representation and living standards  the smoldering aftermath of a gas  station set on fire by protesters in  martinique  an attack that could have been deadly  there are people around here who don't  want to be killed  i don't know what these kids are  thinking setting a gas station on fire  like a bomb that's going too far  martinique and guadalupe have been  gripped for days by heated clashes  between protesters and police  the protests are being fueled by  opposition to france's coronavirus  policies including mandatory vaccination  for health care workers  martinique and guadalupe are both  overseas departments of france  administrative units subject to the same  laws governing the mainland  paris has already pushed back its  deadline for the island's healthcare  workers to be vaccinated  but for many the issue is a reminder  they have limited say over their own  affairs  directly to emmanuel macron  trade unions on the islands have also  been on strike over inequality and  living conditions  france's minister for overseas affairs  has suggested greater autonomy as  something that paris would be willing to  consider  you
 

